  $ pd dns --help || true
  DNS Records — Local service discovery via hostname

  Commands:
    dns register             Register a DNS record
      --hostname <name>      Hostname to register
      --port <n>             Port to resolve to
      --service <id>         Associated service identity

    dns lookup <hostname>    Resolve a hostname to port
    dns list                 List all DNS records
    dns cleanup              Clean stale DNS records
    dns status               DNS system status

  Examples:
    pd dns register --hostname api.local --port <PORT> --service myapp:api
    pd dns lookup api.local

  $ pd services | sed -n '1,12p'

  ID                                 PORT    STATUS      URL
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  port-daddy:api:main                3100    assigned    http://localhost:<PORT>
  port-daddy:website:dev             3101    assigned    http://localhost:<PORT>
  port-daddy:worker:main             3102    assigned    http://localhost:<PORT>

  Total: 3 service(s)
